id=a52sxq_frame_debug_callers
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: no stack walks for debug strings on every frame
author=kusti420
description=simpleperf of SystemUI's main thread while pulling the shade (9.3.112, 3 pulls): 5.3% of its CPU went into Debug.getCallers() stack walks that only build debug strings. (1) framework View.setRequestedFrameRate(F) (Samsung addition) logs Log.i("View", "setRequestedFrameRate frameRate=... this=... caller=" + Debug.getCallers(5)) on every call, and Compose's AndroidComposeView.dispatchDraw calls it on every draw of every Compose view in every app: 561 such lines were in the log buffer after a few minutes of use, each with a 5-frame stack walk and StringBuilder work on the UI thread. The log statement is removed; the assignment it guards (mPreferredFrameRate = frameRate, under the same sToolkitSetFrameRateReadOnlyFlagValue check) stays exactly as in the stock method. (2) SystemUI QSAnimView.nowWithDebugCallers(I) adds Debug.getCallers(3, n) to the timestamp it stores in AnimViewDebugState (read only by the dumpsys of SecQSImplAnimatorManager) whenever a quick panel view's alpha bucket or visibility changes, i.e. many times per shade pull. It now stores the timestamp alone.
